{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be overseeing your care during this admission. You're here for your seventh cycle of high-dose methotrexate for the lymphoma in your brain. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hello, Doctor. I’m feeling okay overall. A bit tired, but no headaches or vision problems. My back pain is the usual, and my ostomy has been more active lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks for letting me know. We saw in your labs that your magnesium is low, which can happen with high ostomy output. We’ll start IV fluids and give you some magnesium to correct that before we begin chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that makes sense. I did try taking more magnesium pills, but it made me nauseous and increased the output. So I cut back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good call. We’ll manage it more carefully with IVs this time. We also noticed your white blood cell count is low. That’s common with chemo, but we’ll monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that delay the chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We want to make sure your counts are stable. We’ll check them again tomorrow. For now, focus on resting and staying hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. And my diabetes meds—should I keep taking metformin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll hold the metformin while you’re here, just like last time. We’ll use insulin if your sugars go up. It’s safer with the chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my thyroid and asthma meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2152-03-31 17:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep taking your levothyroxine daily. For asthma, use your albuterol if you feel tightness. But so far, your breathing sounds clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are back. The magnesium is improving with the IV, but your white count dipped a bit more overnight. We’ll wait one more day before starting chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that going to be a problem? I was hoping to get it done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But giving chemo when your counts are too low increases infection risk. We’ll recheck this afternoon. If it stabilizes, we can proceed tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust your judgment. Any other tests today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We sent a stool test to check for infections since your ostomy output is high. It came back negative for C. diff, parasites, and viruses. So it’s likely related to your magnesium and chemo history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it was another infection like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2152-04-01 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re being cautious. We also tested for CMV, which can affect the gut, but that was negative too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Update: your white count has stabilized. It’s still low, but not dropping. We’re comfortable proceeding with chemo tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! Will it be the same dose as last few times?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 3.5 grams per square meter. We reduced it after the severe mucositis you had at the higher dose. This one has been much better tolerated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that. I don’t want to go through that again. Will I get the leucovorin after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’ll start leucovorin 24 hours after the infusion to protect you. We’ll also give IV bicarbonate to help flush the methotrexate out through your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2152-04-01 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, plenty of IV fluids throughout. We’ll keep you well-hydrated to protect your kidneys and help clear the drug."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2152-04-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Today’s the day. We’re going to start the methotrexate infusion in about an hour. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2152-04-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still feeling okay. A little anxious, but ready to get it done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2152-04-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ll monitor you closely. The nurse will check your vitals every few hours and we’ll draw blood to track the methotrexate levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2152-04-02 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Infusion is complete. You tolerated it very well—no nausea, no drop in blood pressure. Great job."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2152-04-02 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I didn’t feel much at all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2152-04-02 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly what we want. We’ll keep the IV fluids going and start bicarbonate. Tomorrow, we’ll begin leucovorin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2152-04-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your methotrexate level is coming down as expected. We’ve started oral leucovorin—two tablets every six hours for three doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2152-04-03 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I take that at home too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2152-04-03 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll take three more doses at home. We’ll send six tablets with you—take two every six hours, starting from the first dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2152-04-03 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds—can I restart metformin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2152-04-03 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We’ll wait until your methotrexate level is undetectable. We’ll check again tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2152-04-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Quick update: your latest methotrexate level is 0.08. Still a bit high, so we’ll keep monitoring. You’re doing well otherwise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2152-04-03 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2152-04-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s trending down. We expect it to be below 0.05 by tomorrow, which is when we can safely discharge you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2152-04-04 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news. Your methotrexate level is now 0.03—below the threshold. Your kidneys are handling it well, and your counts are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2152-04-04 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2152-04-04 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll discharge you later this morning. We’ll review your meds and give you instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Here’s your discharge plan. You’ll continue leucovorin at home for three doses. Restart metformin as two 500 mg tablets in the morning and two at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s different from before. I was taking 1000 mg at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re adjusting it to reduce GI side effects. Also, start taking magnesium oxide—one tablet twice daily. That should help without worsening ostomy output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, and my pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue methadone, oxycodone as needed, and we’ve switched pregabalin to bedtime only to help with sleep and nerve pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your oncologist in a week. They’ll review your progress and plan the next steps. Call if you develop fever, mouth sores, or severe diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2152-04-04 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before discharge. You’re alert, walking well, and your vitals are stable. All set to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nurse will bring your discharge paperwork and prescriptions. Someone will assist you to the car."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you at your next appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, you too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2152-04-05 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2152-03-31 17:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2152-04-05 15:53:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for her seventh cycle of high-dose methotrexate for diffuse large B-cell lymphoma with CNS involvement. Due to recent high ostomy output and hypomagnesemia, she was initially hydrated with IV fluids and given IV magnesium replacement. Chemotherapy was delayed by one day due to worsening neutropenia, but proceeded when counts stabilized. Methotrexate was administered at 3.5 g/m² and well tolerated. Leucovorin rescue was started 24 hours post-infusion, and methotrexate levels declined appropriately, falling below 0.05 before discharge. Stool studies were negative for infection. Her diabetes was managed by holding metformin during admission, and she was discharged home with medication adjustments, including a revised metformin dose and new magnesium supplementation, along with three doses of oral leucovorin.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Common variable immunodeficiency",
      "Disorders of magnesium metabolism",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Diarrhea",
      "Colostomy status",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Backache, unspecified",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
